{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 45, :comments ["<b>A resident alien</b> — this is a ger toshav. <b>A hired servant</b> — this is a gentile. Now what is the Scriptural derivation [for this distinction], seeing that they are uncircumcised? Rather, it refers to such cases as a circumcised Arab or a circumcised Gibeonite. This is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Exodus 12:45). But I do not know why the Rav would record matters that have been pushed aside [rejected] in the Gemara, for they raised an objection to this very point (Yevamot 71a): but these are circumcised! And they taught in a Mishnah (Nedarim 3:11): one who vows [to abstain] from the uncircumcised is permitted with uncircumcised Israelites but forbidden with the circumcised of the nations of the world, as it is stated (Jeremiah 9:25), 'for all the nations are uncircumcised, and all the house of Israel are uncircumcised of heart.' And they established the verse as referring to a ger who circumcised but did not immerse."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:06:59.443746345Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}